  "name": "365-Day Run Readiness · Part 2: Run-Walk (Weeks 33–52)",
  "description": "365 days. One rule: show up. This is the home stretch.\n\nPart 2 (Weeks 33–52) is where the year pays off: you go from brisk walking to running 45 minutes without stopping, one easy interval at a time. No sprints, no race pace. Every run is conversational and every week builds on the last.\n\nStart here when Part 1 is done and you can brisk-walk 60 minutes comfortably. Not there yet? Keep the strength days and swap the runs for 40–60 minutes of low-impact cardio until you are. The challenge is the daily habit, not the milestone.\n\nThe week: run-walk intervals Monday, Wednesday and Friday, two full-body strength days to keep you strong and injury-free, an easy walk, bike or hike on Saturday and a recovery walk on Sunday. Still something every day.\n\nThe run progression (update the jogging sets and seconds in your copy each week):\nWeeks 33–36: 1–2 min run / 2 min walk × 6–8\nWeeks 37–40: 3–5 min run / 2 min walk × 4–6\nWeeks 41–44: 6–10 min run / 2 min walk × 3–4\nWeeks 45–48: 12–20 min runs with short walk breaks\nWeeks 49–52: continuous easy runs, 25 min building to 45 min\nEvery fourth week is a recovery week. Repeat any week that doesn't feel comfortable. 3 miles steady is the target; 5 is a bonus.\n\nDay 365: an easy 15-minute walk, 10 minutes of mobility and a moment to look back at a year of showing up. That's the real finish line.",
